The cross-section at the resonance peak is given by
$$
\sigma = \frac{2 J + 1}{(2 J_{\mathrm{p}} + 1) (2 J_{\overline{\mathrm{p}}} + 1)} \pi \lambda^{2} \frac{\Gamma_{\mathrm{p}} \Gamma}{(E - M)^{2} + \frac{\Gamma^{2}}{4}}
$$
When $E = M$, resonance occurs. Assuming the resonance state has a spin $J = 0$, and $J_{\mathrm{p}} = 1/2$,
