Method two: This problem is essentially about the Doppler effect, solved using the Doppler formula.

Taking the air as the reference frame, the wave source is stationary, emitting waves at frequency $\nu_{0}$, and the observer is stationary relative to the wind tunnel but moves towards the wave source at speed $v$ in the air reference frame, hearing a sound wave frequency $\nu$,

\[
\nu = \frac{c+v}{c} \nu_{0}
\]

where $c$ is the speed of sound in still air.

\[
\begin{gathered}
c = \frac{\lambda}{T} = \frac{\lambda_{0}}{T_{0}}, \quad c = \lambda \nu = \lambda_{0} \nu_{0} \\
\frac{T}{T_{0}} = \frac{\lambda}{\lambda_{0}} = \frac{\nu_{0}}{\nu} = \frac{c}{c+v} = \frac{1}{1 + \frac{v}{c}}
\end{gathered}
\]

