Hamiltonian $H = -\frac{\hbar^{2}}{2 m} \nabla^{2} + \frac{1}{2} k x^{2} - q F x$

$$
\begin{aligned}
&= -\frac{\hbar^{2}}{2 m} \nabla^{2} + \frac{1}{2} k \left(x - \frac{q F}{k}\right)^{2} - \frac{q^{2} F^{2}}{2 k} \\
&= -\frac{\hbar^{2}}{2 m} \nabla^{\prime 2} + \frac{1}{2} k x^{\prime 2} - \frac{q^{2} F^{2}}{2 k}
\end{aligned}
$$

where $x^{\prime} = x - \frac{q F}{k}$. Thus, the energy level shift is

$$
E^{\prime} = \frac{q^{2} F^{2}}{2 k} = \frac{e^{2} F^{2}}{2 k}
$$

problem:
The HCl molecule has a near-infrared spectral band, where the wavenumbers of adjacent spectral lines are \(	ilde{
u}_{1} = 2925.78 \ \mathrm{cm}^{-1}, \ 	ilde{
u}_{2} = 2906.25 \ \mathrm{cm}^{-1}, \ 	ilde{
u}_{3} = 2865.09 \ \mathrm{cm}^{-1}, \ 	ilde{
u}_{4} = 2843.56 \ \mathrm{cm}^{-1}\), and \(	ilde{
u}_{5} = 2821.49 \ \mathrm{cm}^{-1}.\) The atomic masses of H and Cl are 1.008 and 35, respectively. Given \(h = 6.58 	imes 10^{-22} \ \mathrm{MeV} \cdot \mathrm{s}, \ \mathrm{u} = 1.66 	imes 10^{-27} \ \mathrm{kg}\). Calculate the moment of inertia of this molecule.

solution:
The moment of inertia about the axis in the direction of vector \(\boldsymbol{n}\) passing through the origin is

\[
\begin{aligned}
