For an isolated system, the quantity $E^{2}-c^{2} p^{2}$ is invariant before and after the reaction across different reference frames. The left side of the equation considers the pre-reaction state using the laboratory frame of reference, while the right side considers the post-reaction state using the center-of-momentum frame, where all final state particles are at rest.

Reaction:
$$
\begin{gathered}
\mathrm{p}+\mathrm{p} \rightarrow \mathrm{p}+(\mathrm{p}+4 \pi) \\
