$$
\psi_{m}(\varphi) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}} e^{\mathrm{i} m \varphi}, \quad E_{m} = \frac{m^{2} \hbar^{2}}{2 I}, \quad m = 0, \pm 1, \pm 2, \cdots
$$

The wave function at any time $t$ is:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\psi(\varphi, t) &= \sum_{m} c_{m} \mathrm{e}^{-\mathrm{i} \frac{E_{m} t}{\hbar}} \frac{\mathrm{e}^{\mathrm{i} m \varphi}}{\sqrt{2\pi}}, \\
\psi(\varphi, 0) &= \sum_{m} \frac{c_{m} \mathrm{e}^{\mathrm{i} m \varphi}}{\sqrt{2\pi}}= \begin{cases} \sqrt{\frac{2}{\varphi_{0}}} \sin \frac{\pi \varphi}{\varphi_{0}}, & 0 \leqslant \varphi < \varphi_{0} \\ 0, & \varphi_{0} \leqslant \varphi < 2\pi \end{cases}
\end{aligned}
$$

Where the coefficients are:

$$
\begin{aligned}
& c_{m}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\pi \varphi_{0}}} \int_{0}^{\varphi_{0}} \mathrm{e}^{-\mathrm{i} m \varphi} \sin \frac{\pi \varphi}{\varphi_{0}} \mathrm{~d} \varphi \\
& c_{0}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\pi \varphi_{0}}} \int_{0}^{\varphi_{0}} \sin \frac{\pi \varphi}{\varphi_{0}} \mathrm{~d} \varphi=\frac{2 \varphi_{0}}{\pi \sqrt{\pi \varphi_{0}}}
\end{aligned}
$$

The probability that the particle remains in the ground state is $\left|c_{0}\right|^{2} = \frac{4 \varphi_{0}}{\pi^{3}}$.

