Note that the radial wave function $R(r)$ for the hydrogen atom satisfies the equation

$$
\left[-\frac{\hbar^{2}}{2m} \cdot \frac{1}{r^{2}} \cdot \frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}r}\left(r^{2} \frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}r}\right)+\frac{l(l+1) \hbar^{2}}{2mr^{2}}+V(r)\right] R=E R
$$

Substituting with $R(r)=\chi(r) / r$ and setting $l=0$, we get

\begin{equation*}
