The equations for the center of mass motion and the angular momentum theorem are:

\[
\begin{align*}
\left. m \ddot{y}_{\text{C}} \right|_{\theta=\theta_{0}} & = N - mg \tag{1} \\
\left. \frac{1}{12} m l^{2} \ddot{\theta} \right|_{\theta=\theta_{0}} & = N \cdot \frac{l}{2} \sin \theta_{0} \tag{2}
\end{align*}
\]

Solve the differential equation over a period:

\[
\begin{gathered}
\dot{y}_{A}=\dot{y}_{\text{C}}+\frac{l}{2} \dot{\theta} \sin \theta \\
\ddot{y}_{A}=\ddot{y}_{\text{C}}+\frac{1}{2} l \ddot{\theta} \sin \theta + \frac{1}{2} l \dot{\theta}^{2} \cos \theta
\end{gathered}
\]

At \(\theta = \theta_{0}\), \(\dot{\theta} = 0\), so

\[
\left. \ddot{y}_{A} \right|_{\theta=\theta_{0}} = \left. \ddot{y}_{\text{C}} \right|_{\theta=\theta_{0}} + \left. \frac{1}{2} l \ddot{\theta} \right|_{\theta=\theta_{0}} \sin \theta_{0}=0 \tag{3}
\]

Eliminate \(\left. \ddot{y}_{\text{C}} \right|_{\theta=\theta_{0}}\) and \(\left. \ddot{\theta} \right|_{\theta=\theta_{0}}\) from equation (3) using equations (1) and (2),

\[
\begin{gathered}
\frac{N}{m} - g + \frac{1}{2} l \left( \frac{6N}{ml} \sin \theta_{0} \right) \sin \theta_{0} = 0 \\
N = \frac{mg}{1 + 3 \sin^{2} \theta_{0}}
\end{gathered}
\]

