For the reaction $^{7} \mathrm{Li}+\mathrm{p} \rightarrow { }^{7} \mathrm{Be}+\mathrm{n}+Q$, the reaction energy $Q$ is:
$$
\begin{gathered}
Q=\left(\Delta(^{7} \mathrm{Li})+\Delta(^{1} \mathrm{H})-\Delta(^{7} \mathrm{Be})-\Delta(^{1} \mathrm{n})\right) \\
=14907+7289-15769-8071=-1644 \, \mathrm{keV}
\end{gathered}
$$
This means that in the center-of-mass frame, the relative kinetic energy of $^{7} \mathrm{Li}$ and $\mathrm{p}$ must reach 1644 keV for the reaction $^{7} \mathrm{Li}(\mathrm{p}, \mathrm{n})^{7} \mathrm{Be}$ to occur. Let $E$ be the threshold kinetic energy of the proton in the laboratory frame, and $\boldsymbol{p}$ its momentum. The relation is given by:
$$
\left(E+m_{\mathrm{p}} c^{2}+m_{\mathrm{Li}} c^{2}\right)^{2}-c^{2} p^{2}=\left(|Q|+m_{\mathrm{p}} c^{2}+m_{\mathrm{Li}} c^{2}\right)^{2}
$$
Since $Q \ll m_{\mathrm{p}} c^{2}, \, E \ll m_{\mathrm{p}} c^{2}, \, p^{2}=2 m_{\mathrm{p}} E$, substituting into the above equation gives:
$$
\begin{gathered}
\left(E+m_{\mathrm{p}} c^{2}+m_{\mathrm{Li}} c^{2}\right)^{2}-\left(|Q|+m_{\mathrm{p}} c^{2}+m_{\mathrm{Li}} c^{2}\right)^{2}=2 m_{\mathrm{p}} c^{2} E \\
2\left(m_{\mathrm{p}} c^{2}+m_{\mathrm{Li}} c^{2}\right)(E-|Q|) \approx 2 m_{\mathrm{p}} c^{2} E \\
E=\frac{m_{\mathrm{p}}+m_{\mathrm{Li}}}{m_{\mathrm{Li}}} \times |Q| \approx \frac{1+7}{7} \times 1644=1879 \, \mathrm{keV}
\end{gathered}
$$
The reaction $^{7} \mathrm{Li}(\mathrm{p}, \mathrm{n})^{7} \mathrm{Be}$ can only occur when the kinetic energy of the proton in the laboratory frame exceeds 1879 keV.

