From the eigenvalue equation $\hat{F} \psi(x)=f \psi(x)$, we have

\begin{equation*}  
f(x) \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} f^{*}\left(x^{\prime}\right) \psi\left(x^{\prime}\right) \mathrm{d} x^{\prime}=f \psi(x) \tag{1}  
\end{equation*}  

A solution to equation (1) is $\psi_{0}(x)=c f(x)$, with the corresponding eigenvalue

$$
f_{0}=\int |f(x)|^{2} \mathrm{~d} x > 0
$$
